      "explanation": "The second stage of labour in a primigravida mother typically lasts 1–2 hours (up to 3 hours at most) from complete cervical dilation to delivery of the baby. The provided options (12–20 hours) are physiologically implausible for the second stage; these ranges more closely approximate the duration of the first stage of labour in primigravida. Without access to the source PDF to verify exam-specific framing, no defensible option can be chosen from the given choices.",
